{"title":"Career Roadmap: Layout Artist","role":"Layout Artist","summary":"Career Domain: Media, Communication, Arts & Design · Qualification Pathway: BFA – Applied Art / Visual Communication · Target Career: Layout Artist","facts":{"Current degree":"BFA (Bachelor of Fine Arts)","Course":"Applied Art / Visual Communication"},"about":[{"label":"About this roadmap","text":"This roadmap was drafted with AI assistance from OneGrasp's related roadmaps and is awaiting expert review. Check fees, dates, eligibility and exam patterns on the official websites before you rely on them."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Layout Artist arranges text and images on pages and screens - magazines, books, packaging, ads - so they are clear, balanced and ready for production."},{"type":"h","text":"What a Layout Artist does"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lay out pages to a grid and style guide"},{"text":"Place and edit images and text"},{"text":"Prepare files for print and digital"},{"text":"Check proofs for errors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Where they work:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Publishers and newspapers"},{"text":"Ad agencies"},{"text":"Packaging and print firms"},{"text":"Freelance"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career stage","Typical role"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry-level"},{"text":"Junior Layout Artist"}],[{"text":"Early career"},{"text":"Layout Artist"}],[{"text":"Mid-level"},{"text":"Senior Designer"}],[{"text":"Senior"},{"text":"Art Editor"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Design Head"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Learning Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1: Basics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Typography, grids and composition"},{"text":"Learn InDesign"},{"text":"Study well-designed magazines and books"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2: Production"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Learn print prod